I am working on a folksonomy application
Synonymy (car vs auto vs vehicle)
Polysemy (bank -> river or finance)
No hierarchy (dog picture tagged as #pet #golden-retriever #dog), searches miss
Personal tags don’t work (#toread #my_project)
spam

I was thinking of decoupling the hashtag slug from the entity (see slugs table in schema). Making it a competitive dynamic for which collection wins the tag. So if someone disagrees with a membership, they can fork and propose a new one, owners of tags curate them. What do you think of that?


It does mean that #Jedi could change out from under you, i.e. urls aren't stable.... But you could link to the entity UUID if you wanted.. and #Jedi wouldn't be stable for the specific owners collection, but it would always point to Jedi...DNS: google.com can point to different IPsGit: 'main' branch can move, but commit SHAs are foreverWikipedia: Current version vs permalink to revision


For a topic like #Jedi, imagine the battle between those who only accept the original trilogy, those who include the Disney canon, and those who want to include the "Legends" expanded universe. Your system turns a content dispute into a direct conflict over the platform's primary navigation. How are these disputes resolved?

Voting. Voting on the shape of folksonomy is one of the main ways people enjoy interacting with the site. There is a table that connects entities to slugs. The one with the most votes wins.



